%N A399334 The binomial matrix of the middle binomial coefficients, square array read by ascending antidiagonals.
%C A399334 See the comments and links in A399000.
%H A399334 Peter Luschny, <a href="https://github.com/PeterLuschny/Gists/blob/main/GnomonicExpansionAndBinomialMatrices.ipynb">Gnomonic Expansion and Binomial Matrices</a>, a Python notebook.
%F A399334 A(n, n) = M(n) := binomial(n, floor(n/2)).
%F A399334 A(n, k) = Sum_{m=0..d} binomial(d, m) * s^(d - m) * M(p + m), where d = abs(n - k), p = min(n, k), s = 1 if k <= n, otherwise -1.
